  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nGenerally, the region will experience a warming trend with\ncontinued dry conditions through the rest of the holiday week.\nThis will be due to a building ridge of high pressure that will\nbuild and subsequently translate across the western US through\nThursday. \n\nBy Friday and into the weekend, a trough and upper-level low\npressure system could move into the region. By this time in the\nforecast, confidence lowers and the range of potential solutions\nincreases, which means that it is too soon to pin down any hard\nnumbers for potential of precipitation over the weekend. As this\nlow moves in, temperatures would return back down to normal for\nthis time of year as well. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nThere were no major deviations to the base forecast for this\nafternoon's forecast. With respect to forecast confidence, there\nis a medium-high (~75%) confidence in the expected ridging and \nwarming trend, and lower (~25%) confidence in troughing and \npotential precipitation through the coming weekend.\n\nCliff",
